// one in six); NATURAL BRIDGES of rock from a pier of one row to a pier of the other where two stand within 10 m
// of one another along the nave (thick, unequal, rough under: one on 203 of those seeds, two on 43, none on 54);
// the roof rises in a low vault along it; to one hand of the nave, where the lake has room, the roof rises into ONE
// ROUND SIDE CAVE (dealt); beyond the rows the aisles' piers stand by a lattice of their own (dealt), and the
