// three warm lamps on posts), the widest shaft falling from a broad mouth ringed in dressed stone beside it.
// THE LENS MAY PASS THROUGH A WELL'S SHAFT OF LIGHT (a soft volume); of a well in its way the line asks only its
// bodies: where a rope and its bucket's travel would hang within the lane, that well lets down no rope (counted,
