// IS ASKED); above ground, where that would have left out more than a few things, the line was moved; under the
// rock, SAID PLAINLY: THE LINE TAKES THE ROPES AND BUCKETS OF THE LESSER WELLS IT PASSES UNDER. The turn in the
// chamber passes under the houses round the court and takes the ropes of about three of their wells a seed (941
