// on seed 18): 1,163 of the 90,622 wells of those seeds. Each keeps its mouth, its light and its pool. A thing so left out is
// counted at its own test (info.OUT, by kind) and KEEPS ITS LOT: its footprint stays in the plan's book, bare, and a
// plant keeps its slot in its list at size nought, so the plan is the same plan with or without the line.
//
// THE PLACE STANDS. WHAT IS DRIVEN BY WHAT:
// - by the WORLD'S CLOCK, each from a phase dealt to it on its own stream, whether we are there or not: the sails,
//   the water wheels, the pulleys, the pump beams, the drills, the lifting wheel, the chains' wheels and pots, every
//   bucket with its rope and its thread of water, the people's bending at their work, the walkers and beasts on the
//   road (out and back, each on its own length), the three boats' and the hall's moored skiffs' rocking at their moorings, the
//   wind's bearing (the vanes), the awnings and the washing, the run and sparkle of water (the white of falling
//   water with it), the rings on the lake (each well's from its own bucket's touch; the drips' each on its own
//   period), the net of ripples on the rock, the dust, motes and rain in the shafts of daylight, the lap at the
//   shore, the kit's palms and thorn in the wind, the pigeons, the fish. (The
//   storks stand. There are no swallows.)
// - by the VISIT (the seed and ctx.vary), standing from the first frame to the last: the hour (a forenoon, golden,
//   dawn or night: one sky, one light above, one light below, the slant of the shafts and of the shadows, lanterns
